WEBVTT

00:03.140 --> 00:08.640
At this rate, the first-years 
are going to boycott the club.

00:09.800 --> 00:12.050
I look forward to working 
with you again today.

02:01.640 --> 02:02.570
Whoops.

02:02.570 --> 02:04.340
Sir...

02:04.340 --> 02:05.590
Are you all right?

02:05.890 --> 02:07.150
I'm sorry.

02:07.150 --> 02:10.310
My legs ache lately.

02:16.860 --> 02:19.860
<b>Tsukinaga Family</b>

02:20.910 --> 02:24.870
<b>Episode 4</b>

02:20.910 --> 02:24.870
<b>Etude With You</b>

02:26.880 --> 02:28.110
Okay, stop.

02:28.120 --> 02:29.750
<b>Sunrise Festival</b>

02:28.850 --> 02:31.270
<i>Three days until the Sunrise Festival.</i>

02:31.700 --> 02:36.840
<i>It's the home stretch, and competition 
practice is picking up pace.</i>

02:37.580 --> 02:41.940
<i>We took hardly any time 
to rest between practice.</i>

02:45.090 --> 02:46.080
So heavy...

02:46.080 --> 02:48.480
My legs are so swollen.

02:48.480 --> 02:53.500
I heard you saved the day again with 
Sally-chan, unbeknownst to everyone.

02:53.500 --> 02:56.130
I just heard her out.

02:56.130 --> 02:57.750
I doubt that.

02:57.750 --> 02:59.740
Ririka was impressed, too.

02:59.740 --> 03:01.430
Yeah, right.

03:01.430 --> 03:04.990
If anything, I'm fed up with 
how little I can help.

03:05.840 --> 03:09.740
You've changed a bit since you 
became the president, haven't you?

03:10.350 --> 03:12.010
Have I?

03:12.010 --> 03:14.140
You haven't changed, though, Kanade-chan.

03:14.140 --> 03:17.330
I'll take that as a compliment.

03:17.330 --> 03:20.730
Still, you don't need to say that out loud!

03:25.280 --> 03:26.800
What's wrong?

03:26.800 --> 03:29.530
Well, my senpai in charge of management

03:29.530 --> 03:32.300
asked me to make sure there are 
no mistakes in our roster.

03:32.300 --> 03:35.360
And you got yelled at 
for saying "Tsukinaga."

03:35.360 --> 03:37.800
No, well...

03:37.800 --> 03:40.780
I like the last name Tsukinaga, though.

03:40.780 --> 03:41.870
Scary!

03:41.870 --> 03:43.720
Go away, Kanade-chan.

03:44.380 --> 03:45.530
Fine, fine.

03:45.530 --> 03:48.750
You shouldn't do that, Motomu-kun.

03:50.300 --> 03:51.200
Sorry.

04:01.320 --> 04:04.770
It's been a while since the 
four of us went home together.

04:05.140 --> 04:06.690
It has.

04:07.260 --> 04:08.460
Motomu-kun?

04:08.460 --> 04:09.580
Yes.

04:09.580 --> 04:13.320
He's been acting a bit weird during 
practice since around last week.

04:13.320 --> 04:15.120
He has?

04:15.120 --> 04:18.060
I thought he's always been that way.

04:18.070 --> 04:21.440
Higuchi: At least say hi before our
performance at Sunrise Festival. 
Gen-chan-sensei's really worried 
about you.

04:18.670 --> 04:23.000
He's only ever really talked to Midori.

04:23.000 --> 04:24.070
Is he shy?

04:24.070 --> 04:28.640
More like he doesn't trust people.

04:28.640 --> 04:30.790
He's cautious.

04:30.790 --> 04:32.000
Cautious?

04:32.000 --> 04:33.160
Could it be...

04:33.610 --> 04:36.850
That he's royalty in some other nation?

04:36.850 --> 04:38.570
No way.

04:38.570 --> 04:39.510
It's just...

04:39.510 --> 04:41.710
Gen'ichiro Tsukinaga.

04:41.710 --> 04:43.430
That's right.

04:43.430 --> 04:47.530
Motomu-kun stayed home with 
family issues last week.

04:47.530 --> 04:50.640
Something might have happened.

04:50.640 --> 04:53.130
Gen'ichiro? Who's that?

04:53.470 --> 04:55.350
Tsukinaga Gen'ichiro.

04:55.350 --> 04:58.190
He's a famous instructor in the 
high school concert band scene.

04:58.480 --> 05:03.330
He signed up as the advisor at Ryusei Academy 
last year and took them to the Nationals.

05:01.070 --> 05:03.650
Go for the Nationals!

05:01.070 --> 05:03.650
<b>Concert Band Life</b>

05:01.070 --> 05:03.650
<b>Kyoto\h\h\h\h\hRyusei Academy High School</b>

05:03.330 --> 05:05.640
Is that the boys' school?

05:05.640 --> 05:10.960
Motomu-kun was practically guaranteed a spot 
in high school after Ryusei Middle School.

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
