Kyoto</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Inan Setsuriku</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Chisato University
High School</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Amagasaki Sousei</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Ibaraki Academy</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Kitakawa Dai-ni</b>

05:07.660 --> 05:14.660
<b>Ryusei Academy</b>

05:10.960 --> 05:13.460
But he transferred to Kitauji.

05:13.460 --> 05:14.660
He was?

05:14.660 --> 05:17.530
That must have something to do with it.

05:17.530 --> 05:19.920
It's fine if no one knows about it,

05:20.230 --> 05:24.750
but there are people like Kanade-chan 
who happen to know something's up.

05:24.750 --> 05:26.900
That makes things more complicated.

05:26.900 --> 05:30.590
Motomu-kun's never told 
you anything about it?

05:31.350 --> 05:34.790
I thought it might not be good 
to ask just out of curiosity.

05:35.770 --> 05:37.390
Tsukinaga, huh?

05:37.390 --> 05:41.950
Since they have the same last name,
they must be related or something, right?

05:41.950 --> 05:43.430
I think so.

05:43.430 --> 05:47.540
That must be why he hates being 
called by his last name so much.

05:48.070 --> 05:50.720
Maybe they don't get along or something.

05:50.720 --> 05:54.380
I think it's a bit much to switch 
schools because of that, though.

05:55.640 --> 06:01.530
Wait, isn't Ryusei right after 
us in the Sunrise Festival?

06:07.340 --> 06:08.240
You're right.

06:07.340 --> 06:11.470
<b>Ryukyo</b>

06:07.340 --> 06:11.470
<b>Kitauji</b>

06:07.340 --> 06:11.470
<b>Ryusei
Academy</b>

06:07.340 --> 06:11.470
<b>Rikka</b>

06:07.340 --> 06:11.470
<b>Suishouzaka</b>

06:08.240 --> 06:10.060
Could that be a problem?

06:10.060 --> 06:13.430
He was pretty pissed today.

06:13.430 --> 06:15.970
I don't think that'll be an issue.

06:16.830 --> 06:19.730
Motomu-kun loves music.

06:19.730 --> 06:22.390
He won't do anything to 
disrupt the performance.

06:22.390 --> 06:25.160
I think we can trust him.

06:25.160 --> 06:30.540
<i>With that, we decided to stop 
prying and just keep an eye out.</i>

06:32.450 --> 06:35.710
<i>And then, the Sunrise Festival was upon us.</i>

06:39.060 --> 06:41.760
All right, everyone, listen up.

06:42.590 --> 06:46.540
Be sure to do your final checks 
before you enter the stadium.

06:46.540 --> 06:52.760
We worked ridiculously hard up until 
now. All that's left is to perform.

06:48.040 --> 06:51.150
So that's President Azusa Sasaki 
that I've heard rumors about.

06:51.150 --> 06:52.220
Rumors?

06:52.760 --> 06:58.610
I heard from my friend that you and President 
Sasaki from Rikka High School were close.

06:58.610 --> 07:00.950
We were in middle school.

07:01.240 --> 07:04.810
Did you never think about 
going to Rikka High School?

07:04.810 --> 07:09.160
I wasn't sure I'd be doing concert band.

07:09.430 --> 07:11.530
And yet, you're the president now.

07:11.530 --> 07:13.000
I like that.

07:13.000 --> 07:16.220
I think it's beautiful that 
you don't try to resist fate.

07:16.220 --> 07:18.280
I can't tell if you're throwing 
shade at me right now.

07:18.280 --> 07:20.890
All right! Let's do this!

07:21.380 --> 07:24.510
If we aren't smiling, we aren't Rikka!

07:24.890 --> 07:25.920
We enjoy...

07:25.920 --> 07:27.010
...music!

07:27.010 --> 07:28.260
We love...

07:28.260 --> 07:29.410
...music!

07:29.410 --> 07:30.960
We are...

07:30.960 --> 07:33.210
...Rikka!

07:35.210 --> 07:37.820
Aren't we going to come up 
with something like that?

07:37.820 --> 07:39.040
We already have one.

07:39.040 --> 07:41.050
Go, Kitauji!

07:41.050 --> 07:43.310
<i>That</i> thing?

07:42.650 --> 07:45.050
Look, it's the Kitauji president.

07:47.810 --> 07:50.450
Maybe it's the unexpectedness that matters.

07:50.450 --> 07:51.450
Huh?

07:51.780 --> 07:53.710
Hey, it's Ryusei.

07:54.620 --> 07:56.590
Thank you in advance.

07:56.590 --> 07:59.170
I look forward to it.

08:00.690 --> 08:02.760
Their costumes are so awesome.

08:02.760 --> 08:05.210
I guess they're themed after cheer squads.

08:09.680 --> 08:11.430
The length looks about right for you.

08:12.210 --> 08:13.250
What's wrong?

08:13.250 --> 08:14.950
It's torn here.

08:15.950 --> 08:19.280
I told you to lose some more weight!

08:19.280 --> 08:20.520
True...

08:20.520 --> 08:23.750
And now I'm wearing LL pants.

08:23.750 --> 08:25.200
Dammit, don't make me say it!

08:26.550 --> 08:28.490
Did it fray?

08:28.490 --> 08:29.720
Yes.

08:30.660 --> 08:31.860
Over here.

08:32.670 --> 08:36.340
It's just a quick repair, 
but it should hold up.

08:37.270 --> 08:39.240
You're amazing, Mama-senpai!

08:39.240 --> 08:40.810
You're like a mom!

08:42.260 --> 08:46.790
Competition practice overlapped 
with festival practice this year.

08:43.540 --> 08:46.790
Sunrise Festival

08:46.790 --> 08:48.270
I imagine it was difficult.

08:48.870 --> 08:53.090
And yet, you're performing at 
a higher level than last year.

08:53.500 --> 08:57.670
It must be the fruits of the drum major's 
strict coaching and everyone's efforts.

08:58.060 --> 09:03.430
Sunrise Festival draws many locals 
and parents and guardians.

09:04.160 --> 09:07.570
Go show them what you've 
been working so hard on!

09:07.570 --> 09:08.690
Yes!

09:09.150 --> 09:10.310
Well, President.

09:10.310 --> 09:11.080
Err...

09:11.080 --> 09:14.710
Okay, follow my lead, please.

09:14.710 --> 09:16.840
Go, Kitauji!

09:16.840 --> 09:18.190
Yeah!

09:21.270 --> 09:23.820
I'm starting to get nervous.

09:23.820 --> 09:25.250
Don't worry.

09:25.250 --> 09:27.610
We did everything we could.

09:28.890 --> 09:30.150
Motomu!

09:31.160 --> 09:32.390
Higuchi.

09:34.650 --> 09:36.510
You saw my message, didn't you?

09:36.510 --> 09:38.960
Say hi before the performance.

09:38.960 --> 09:40.580
Motomu!

09:40.580 --> 09:42.700
And when did I say I would?

09:42.700 --> 09:44.060
Why not?

09:44.060 --> 09:46.610
Gen-chan-sensei's really worried.

09:46.610 --> 09:48.090
Not my problem.

09:48.090 --> 09:49.570
It is!

09:49.910 --> 09:52.420
Gen-chan-sensei is your grandfa—

09:52.420 --> 09:53.030
Shut up!

09:55.170 --> 09:56.490
Ugh.

09:56.490 --> 10:01.050
A-Anyway, we're all waiting for you.

10:01.820 --> 10:03.360
Motomu-kun.

10:03.360 --> 10:05.990
I'm sorry, I know we're about to perform.

10:05.990 --> 10:08.690
I wish you hadn't seen that, Midori-senpai.

10:35.560 --> 10:37.560
You did great, Takekawa-san.

10:37.560 --> 10:39.630
You nailed it. Maybe more than I did.

10:39.630 --> 10:41.790
I doubt that.

10:41.790 --> 10:43.000
Takekawa-san.

10:46.220 --> 10:47.910
Y-Yes...?

10:47.910 --> 10:49.370
That was fantastic.

10:49.370 --> 10:52.490
Thanks for working so 
hard in so little time.

10:52.850 --> 10:59.260
I think everyone was inspired by 
how well you performed as a beginner.

11:00.340 --> 11:03.750
Thank you... so much.

11:04.810 --> 11:07.580
Try to make it in the competition.

11:07.580 --> 11:08.810
I'm looking forward to seeing you there.

11:08.810 --> 11:09.900
Right!

11:14.540 --> 11:15.910
Thanks.

11:15.910 --> 11:18.060
You were listening?

11:18.060 --> 11:18.640
Yeah.

11:19.380 --> 11:22.200
Your drum majoring was good, too.

11:23.930 --> 11:28.780
It felt like someone finally 
surpassed Asuka-senpai.

11:30.570 --> 11:31.930
That's too much.

11:31.930 --> 11:33.500
But it's true.

11:33.500 --> 11:38.160
The first and second-years were like, 
"Kousaka-senpai's such an angel!"

11:38.800 --> 11:40.120
Stop it!

11:40.120 --> 11:41.990
Sorry.

11:42.460 --> 11:45.000
Sorry, Reina, I'll see you later.

11:48.930 --> 11:50.390
Um...

11:52.560 --> 11:53.930
Kumiko-chan.

11:55.690 --> 11:56.700
I see...

11:57.630 --> 12:03.830
So he hadn't told anyone in Kitauji that 
Gen-chan-sensei is his grandfather.

12:03.830 --> 12:06.400
It's not a common last name,

12:06.400 --> 12:10.180
so I'm sure some of the more 
observant ones noticed something.

12:10.180 --> 12:11.970
Is it really that upsetting?

12:12.260 --> 12:14.970
What's Gen'ichiro-sensei like?

12:14.970 --> 12:16.260
Is he scary?

12:16.260 --> 12:18.000
Huh? Not at all!

12:18.350 --> 12:20.420
He's really easy to talk to.

12:20.420 --> 12:22.390
Everyone looks up to him.

12:22.390 --> 12:25.920
It was thanks to him that we won 
gold in the Nationals last year.

12:25.920 --> 12:27.340
Oh, I see.

12:28.670 --> 12:33.200
More than anything, Gen-chan-sensei's 
really worried about Motomu.

12:33.790 --> 12:37.160
He seems to want to sit 
down and talk to him.

12:37.160 --> 12:41.070
He asked us to tell him if we 
know anything about Motomu.

12:41.070 --> 12:44.070
So it's just Motomu-kun 
that's being that way?

12:44.400 --> 12:45.680
I think so.

12:45.680 --> 12:49.430
So I couldn't help but want 
to do something for him.

12:49.430 --> 12:53.360
So you don't know why 
Motomu-kun's avoiding him?

12:53.360 --> 12:54.860
Not specifically.

12:55.690 --> 12:56.500
But...

12:58.490 --> 13:01.710
I think it might have something 
to do with his big sister.

13:01.710 --> 13:04.250
His sister?

13:04.250 --> 13:07.090
Wait, he hasn't told you about that, either?

13:10.400 --> 13:14.050
His sister passed away.

13:14.050 --> 13:15.270
Three years ago.

13:25.280 --> 13:27.570
His sister passed away from illness.

13:27.570 --> 13:29.970
Motomu became really depressed.

13:29.970 --> 13:35.870
Gen-chan-sensei was worried, so he 
transferred to Ryusei to be close to him.

13:37.000 --> 13:41.570
<i>Part of me thought he'd had a fight
 and a falling out with his grandfather.</i>

13:41.570 --> 13:46.250
<i>I felt ashamed for making 
such an assumption.</i>

13:46.490 --> 13:50.740
I think I was running away from him a bit.

13:50.740 --> 13:52.430
From Motomu-kun?

13:53.270 --> 13:59.010
Right after he joined last year, 
he said he wanted to study under me.

13:59.470 --> 14:01.990
And he's been that way ever since.

14:01.990 --> 14:04.970
I mean, I'd probably want some
space if someone told me

14:04.970 --> 14:07.620
they want me to be their master.

14:09.250 --> 14:15.940
He plays from his heart, though, 
and he aspires to improve.

14:15.940 --> 14:20.960
I can tell that he truly loves 
music and concert band.

14:21.280 --> 14:25.730
Yet he doesn't try to talk 
to anyone besides me.

14:26.110 --> 14:30.090
I figured there must have 
been a reason, but...

14:33.480 --> 14:36.230
I'll try talking to him properly.

14:36.230 --> 14:37.510
Midori-chan...

14:37.820 --> 14:42.140
I've been thinking I need to talk 
to him at some point anyway.

14:43.710 --> 14:44.890
Yeah?

14:45.210 --> 14:46.140
Yes.

14:47.440 --> 14:49.830
It's rough being a senpai, huh?

14:49.830 --> 14:51.200
I know.

14:51.200 --> 14:54.530
When did we even become senpais, anyway?

14:54.530 --> 14:56.290
It crept up on both of us.

14:58.530 --> 14:59.660
That's it.

14:59.660 --> 15:03.380
Change your breath even when you're 
using the same fingering.

15:03.380 --> 15:05.460
That'll change your tone.

15:05.460 --> 15:06.250
Okay.

15:06.960 --> 15:10.060
Huh, the contrabass couple isn't here.

15:10.060 --> 15:12.630
Huh? They were here just a minute ago.

15:12.630 --> 15:14.230
Something's fishy.

15:14.230 --> 15:15.570
Kanade-chan.

15:16.600 --> 15:19.260
Is it about what happened the other day?

15:19.260 --> 15:20.950
So childish.

15:20.950 --> 15:23.300
Anyway, let's start practice.

15:23.630 --> 15:26.450
Why are you siding with Tsukinaga?

15:26.450 --> 15:28.840
He's just being a brat.

15:29.270 --> 15:31.980
Yet everyone's walking 
on eggshells around him.

15:31.980 --> 15:32.910
All right.

15:32.910 --> 15:34.880
I'll hear you out later.

15:35.550 --> 15:38.340
I'm not asking you to hear me out.

15:38.340 --> 15:39.110
I'm just...

15:39.110 --> 15:40.380
How unusual.

15:41.130 --> 15:44.130
Kanade-chan never gets so upset.

15:44.130 --> 15:46.290
She must be really worried about Motomu-kun.

15:46.290 --> 15:48.870
Huh? What are you talking about?!

15:50.050 --> 15:51.960
We're starting practice.

16:00.050 --> 16:01.580
Motomu-kun...

16:02.110 --> 16:03.560
I'm sorry.

16:07.700 --> 16:09.560
Contrabass?

16:09.870 --> 16:10.810
Yes.

16:11.120 --> 16:16.310
I thought it might be good to have 
one more, especially for next year.

16:17.130 --> 16:19.830
Motomu-kun's going to be alone, isn't he?

16:20.160 --> 16:21.200
Yeah.

16:24.510 --> 16:25.690
All right.

16:26.100 --> 16:28.720
Since you're the president, I'll tell you.

16:28.720 --> 16:32.640
Please don't tell the executives about this.

16:32.640 --> 16:34.590
Huh? O-Okay.

16:36.180 --> 16:43.860
Tsukinaga-sensei approached us about 
having Motomu-kun transferred to Ryusei.

16:45.050 --> 16:46.280
And...

16:46.740 --> 16:51.070
Of course, he said he'd like to 
honor Motomu-kun's own wishes.

16:51.720 --> 16:54.810
But this is a family matter.

16:54.810 --> 16:56.780
I don't know how it's going to turn out.

16:56.780 --> 16:59.770
Please just keep that in mind.

17:04.690 --> 17:06.540
What's going to happen now?

17:07.750 --> 17:10.470
In that case, Midori-chan's going to be...

17:12.800 --> 17:14.150
Kumiko-chan.

17:15.420 --> 17:16.190
Midori-chan!

17:16.190 --> 17:18.650
You don't have to get <i>that</i> freaked out.

17:19.840 --> 17:21.220
I see...

17:22.210 --> 17:23.570
Yeah.

17:23.570 --> 17:28.640
I asked him to tell me what 
happened and what's on his mind.

17:29.030 --> 17:31.190
And I promised I wouldn't tell anyone.

17:31.630 --> 17:32.650
But...

17:32.990 --> 17:34.500
I'm sorry.

17:34.920 --> 17:38.240
I won't cause you any more 
trouble going forward.

17:38.470 --> 17:40.700
That's not it.

17:41.310 --> 17:46.690
I guess he doesn't trust me.

17:46.690 --> 17:49.110
I don't think that's what it is.

17:50.180 --> 17:52.090
<i>Should I tell her?</i>

17:52.090 --> 17:54.590
<i>Should I not?</i>

17:54.920 --> 17:59.960
<i>I felt like I was doing something 
nasty just considering it.</i>

17:59.960 --> 18:03.410
<i>I said bye to Midori-chan 
having not told her anything.</i>

18:08.270 --> 18:09.560
Oumae-senpai.

18:11.380 --> 18:13.120
Motomu-kun.

18:15.880 --> 18:19.130
Higuchi told you all that?

18:19.130 --> 18:20.890
Please don't be angry at him.

18:20.890 --> 18:24.830
I practically forced half of it out of him.

18:26.870 --> 18:30.580
Midori-senpai asked me to talk to her today.

18:30.580 --> 18:33.350
Yeah, she told me.

18:33.350 --> 18:36.920
And I heard you're being 
invited to another school.

18:36.920 --> 18:39.860
I guess I shouldn't be surprised 
our president knows everything.

18:41.580 --> 18:44.880
Although there's a lot I wish I didn't know.

18:46.120 --> 18:51.340
I don't hate my grandpa or anything.

18:53.710 --> 18:56.480
We used to be close.

18:59.930 --> 19:05.470
That's why my sister went to 
the school Grandpa taught at.

19:07.830 --> 19:10.630
But being the grandchild of the instructor,

19:11.370 --> 19:16.050
she suffered in ways that had nothing 
to do with playing, like jealousy.

19:19.410 --> 19:26.620
Still, Grandpa tried to choose her to join 
the competition based entirely on her ability.

19:26.620 --> 19:29.720
That just made things even more tense.

19:32.300 --> 19:35.890
She loved concert band so much.

19:37.080 --> 19:41.750
She became sick, and in the 
end, she had no interest...

19:44.500 --> 19:50.280
That's why you didn't want to do 
concert band with your grandfather?

19:50.280 --> 19:51.320
Yes.

19:51.320 --> 19:53.750
I felt like I'd be letting my sister down

19:53.750 --> 19:58.110
if I didn't enjoy concert band 
the way she imagined it'd be.

20:00.290 --> 20:01.380
Ah.

20:01.920 --> 20:03.590
I'm sorry.

20:03.590 --> 20:06.430
You could have told Midori-chan.

20:06.940 --> 20:12.990
I thought about it, but Midori-senpai 
reminds me of my sister.

20:21.140 --> 20:23.440
Seeing Midori-senpai, I think to myself...

20:24.370 --> 20:29.950
This must be the concert 
band that she'd imagined.

20:33.940 --> 20:36.440
She loves music and has fun playing.

20:37.180 --> 20:41.960
She just wants to work on 
her skills with the others.

20:41.960 --> 20:43.640
Hence "master," huh?

20:44.290 --> 20:47.310
Midori-chan's true to herself 
when it comes to music.

20:47.310 --> 20:48.080
Yes.

20:48.080 --> 20:52.470
That's why I want Midori-senpai 
to stay the way she is now.

20:52.930 --> 20:54.010
Got it.

20:56.600 --> 20:57.550
Bye.

20:57.550 --> 21:00.580
Oh, don't worry about me.

21:00.580 --> 21:02.850
I don't plan on going back to Ryusei.

21:02.850 --> 21:09.260
I appreciate that, but first, I want you to 
talk to your grandpa and to Higuchi-kun.

21:10.140 --> 21:13.860
They're both seriously worried about you.

21:14.200 --> 21:17.830
That you might be angry because of them.

21:21.330 --> 21:23.370
Your music is going to 
reflect your state of mind.

21:26.140 --> 21:27.920
Thank you.

21:27.920 --> 21:29.880
For thinking so much of me.

21:31.060 --> 21:36.150
I want to put on the best performance 
we can with the members we have.

21:36.730 --> 21:42.100
I want this to be our best performance 
of the past three years.

21:43.120 --> 21:50.030
So I want you to play well for Kitauji.

21:50.590 --> 21:51.860
That's all.

21:55.790 --> 21:58.370
I really appreciate that.

22:09.890 --> 22:14.560
Today

22:09.890 --> 22:14.560
How are you?

22:10.850 --> 22:14.560
Read

22:13.600 --> 22:14.560
Mamiko

22:13.600 --> 22:14.560
What?

22:15.520 --> 22:16.270
Today

22:15.520 --> 22:16.270
How are you?

22:15.520 --> 22:16.270
Read

22:15.520 --> 22:16.270
Mamiko

22:15.520 --> 22:16.270
What?

22:16.270 --> 22:19.230
What?

22:16.270 --> 22:19.230
As long as you're alive

22:16.480 --> 22:19.230
Read

22:19.310 --> 22:20.690
As long as you're alive

22:19.310 --> 22:20.690
Read

22:19.310 --> 22:20.690
Mamiko

22:19.310 --> 22:20.690
<b>Wha?</b>

22:32.330 --> 22:33.640
Motomu-kun.

22:34.490 --> 22:37.030
I contacted Grandpa and Higuchi.

22:38.390 --> 22:41.930
I told them everything and told 
them I'd be staying here.

22:42.540 --> 22:46.180
This is where I can be myself.

22:46.670 --> 22:47.930
I want to be here.

22:49.610 --> 22:52.370
I belong to Kitauji.

22:58.720 --> 23:00.030
Midori-senpai.

23:01.740 --> 23:03.460
Um, I...

23:03.460 --> 23:04.650
Motomu-kun.

23:06.000 --> 23:08.420
Would you like to play something together?

23:13.840 --> 23:14.700
Okay...

23:15.350 --> 23:17.960
There's a piece I'd like 
you to play with me.

23:19.330 --> 23:24.090
Your instructor will
 have any forgotten items

24:47.840 --> 24:56.010
<b>Agata Festival</b>

24:50.140 --> 24:54.550
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

24:52.010 --> 24:56.010
<b>To be continued</b>
